47 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424047 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424047 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424047 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424047 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424047 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424030 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424047 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "99010428-33fd-5dd7-a898-3d5893398292" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424048 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424026 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424048 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424027 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424048 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424048 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424032 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424048 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424044 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424048 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424048 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424048 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424031 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424048 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d020dc5f-a9e6-5b1f-9ba1-79c84664ccd0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424049 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424025 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424049 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424036 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424049 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424039 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424049 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424049 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424049 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424049 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424049 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424049 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "efac0da0-aee9-5e9c-ae73-a7e2c584348e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424050 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424050 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96334" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424050 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424050 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-3,1],$ compute $P(-2\\le X\\le 2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424050 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2b0137dd-0ad1-53cf-acd8-0bbd632c8d90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424050 #edb/ref 1074 "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-3,1],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}, & -3\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-2\\le X\\le 2) & =P(-2\\le X\\le 1) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{1}\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1-(-2)}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424051 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424047 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424051 #edb/ref 1069 "q-130692" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424051 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424051 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the continuous random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[0,4],$ compute $P(W\\ge 1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424051 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6a51ea05-5e14-5ec8-80f9-413f5ec71214" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424051 #edb/ref 1074 "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $W$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le w\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[0,4],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4},\\, & 0\\le w\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W\\ge 1) & =P(1\\le W\\le 4) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}f(w)\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{4-1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424052 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424052 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96284" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424052 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424052 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the continuous random variable $U$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-10,10],$ compute $P(U<-3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424052 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b864ebe6-e085-5252-a91f-4ca0cb314e2f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424052 #edb/ref 1074 "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $U$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le u\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $U$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-10,10],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(u)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{20},\\, & -10\\le u\\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(U<-3) & =P(-10\\le U<-3) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-10}^{-3}f(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-10}^{-3}\\frac{1}{20}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{-3-(-10)}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424053 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424048 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424053 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96279" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424053 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424053 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the continuous random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[3,10],$ compute $P(W\\le 5).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424053 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b9258154-36aa-5bfe-9428-732732589876" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424053 #edb/ref 1074 "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $W$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le w\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $W$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[3,10],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(w)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{7},\\, & 3\\le w\\le 10, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(W\\le 5) & =P(3\\le W\\le 5) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}f(w)\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{5}\\frac{1}{7}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & =\\frac{5-3}{7} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424054 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186424045 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424054 #edb/ref 1069 "q-96333" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424054 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424054 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the continuous random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ compute $P(0\\le X\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{4}).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424054 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f0228a94-8a4a-532e-880c-3c74fb2a7fa3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186424054 #edb/ref 1074 "The probability density function for a uniformly distributed continuous random variable $X$ on an interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{b-a},\\, & a\\le x\\le b, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOur random variable $X$ is uniformly distributed on the interval $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ so it has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2\\pi },\\, & -\\pi \\le x\\le \\pi , \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le X\\le \\frac{3\\pi }{4}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3\\pi /4}\\frac{1}{2\\pi }\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}-0)}{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
